  "purpose": "eCore publishes no OpenAPI/Swagger document. The framework forbids authoring an endpoint, so this file records what the application itself revealed - the calls it actually made, and the paths it declares in its own markup. It is evidence, never authority.",
  "howToRead": {
    "OBSERVED": "The call was made by the application and its request/response shape was captured. Per SEM-API-CONTRACT an OBSERVED contract may drive a scenario to a state, but may NOT judge an acceptance criterion: asserting against it would make current behaviour the definition of correct and a real regression would pass forever.",
    "UNVERIFIED": "The path is declared by the application but was never exercised here. Nothing about its method, request shape, response shape or side effects is known. It must not appear in an API client until it is observed or approved.",
    "promotion": "OBSERVED or UNVERIFIED becomes HUMAN_APPROVED only by a human decision recorded at Approval Gate 2."
  },
  "credentialHandling": {
    "sessionSource": ".auth/ecore-session.json, written by scripts/ecore-session-capture.ts and git-ignored",
    "ration": "Every value passed to an MCP tool is written into the agent transcript, so the password was never typed through MCP. The seed Playwright project resumes the captured session instead.",
    "recorded": "Paths, methods, status codes, content types, request parameter NAMES and response field NAMES.",
    "neverRecorded": "Credentials, cookies, request/response VALUES, transaction identifiers, customer or user data."
  },

  "baseUrl": {
    "value": "https://qa1.eoriginal.org:8443/ssweb/setup",
    "contractSource": "OBSERVED",
    "note": "Derived from the observed paths, which all share the /ssweb/setup prefix. Deliberately NOT assumed to equal PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL, which points at the login page."
  },

  "architecturalFinding": {
    "summary": "eCore is a server-rendered Java web application, not an API-backed SPA. There is no REST resource model, no JSON request bodies, and no versioned API surface.",
    "evidence": [
      "Sign-in is POST /ssweb/setup/eo_cc_login returning 302 with resourceType 'document'. There is no login endpoint that returns a token or a JSON body.",
      "All primary navigation (Home, New Transaction, Workspace, Preferences) is full document requests. Zero XHR on those page loads except Workspace.",
      "The AJAX endpoints are RPC-style verbs ending in .eo, not resources. Requests are form-encoded, not JSON.",
      "Of the three endpoints observed, one returns an HTML fragment rather than data."
    ],
    "consequenceForTesting": "API testing here can never replace UI testing of a user-facing acceptance criterion, because the endpoints return either presentation markup or presentation-formatted data. Its realistic value is fast state setup and teardown for UI scenarios, not assertion."
  },

